I turn on the television. Find a game. Watch without seeing. The commentators' voices blur into white noise. My hand rests on my thigh. The lace is underneath. Everything is underneath now. The panties. The feelings. The question of what Victoria has planned for tomorrow.

The question of what Adrian has planned for my wife.

I watch the game until Lena turns off her light. Then I watch the highlights. Then I watch the post-game. Then I sit in the dark and feel the panties and think about nothing and everything and the space between the two where I seem to be living now.

